%description:

Tcp.nagleEnabled:on -- a small segment waits while sent data is not acknowledged.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "Nagle's algorithm (RFC 896) enabled/disabled"; RFC 9293 section 3.7.4.

The classes: on (true, the default), off (false), socket-override (TCP_NODELAY of a socket). The code: a segment shorter than the MSS
waits while sent data is not acknowledged (TcpConnection::sendData()). TCP_NODELAY of a
socket takes the place of the parameter for its connection (the class socket-override). This test separates "on" from "off".

Host under test: host1, which writes 100 bytes at 0.2 s and 100 bytes at 0.21 s. Peer: host2,
which acknowledges after its delayed ACK of 200 ms. Observation: level 1, the second segment of
host1 does not go before the ACK of the first one, about 0.2 s later.

%# parameter: Tcp.nagleEnabled
%# class: on
%# value: true
%# key: *.host1.tcp.nagleEnabled
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpNagleEnabledOn")
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
             .describe("the first segment of 100 bytes")
             .within(0.5))
        .never(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
              .filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 101 && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
              .describe("an early second segment of 100 bytes, after the ACK of the first")
              .within(0.15))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 101 && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
             .describe("second segment of 100 bytes, after the ACK of the first")
             .within(0.1));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpNagleEnabledOn compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.nagleEnabled = true    # the parameter under test
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 0B
*.host1.app[0].sendScript = "0.2 100; 0.21 100"
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpNagleEnabledOn: PASS
